const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"在偏差、方差与简洁性之间取舍",en:"Trade bias against variance and complexity"},body:{zh:"普通最小二乘可能具有较大估计方差，完整模型也可能难以解释。Lasso通过收缩系数并让部分系数为零，在预测与简洁性之间寻求取舍。增加偏差有时能降低预测误差，但这不是任何数据都必然改善，更不等于找到了唯一真实模型。",en:"Ordinary least squares can have substantial variance and a full model may be hard to interpret. Lasso shrinks coefficients and sets some to zero, balancing prediction and simplicity. Added bias can sometimes reduce prediction error, but improvement is not universal and the selected model need not be uniquely true."},reference:{url:"https://sites.stat.washington.edu/courses/stat527/s13/readings/j_royal_stat_soc_b1996.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1996年期刊版，第267页",en:"Source: 1996 journal article, pp. 267"}}},{title:{zh:"约束上限越小，收缩越强",en:"A smaller bound means more shrinkage"},body:{zh:"原文最小化残差平方和，同时限制系数绝对值之和不超过t。较小的约束上限通常意味着更强收缩；这与常见惩罚形式中参数越大、惩罚越强的方向不同。比较软件参数时，先确认使用的是约束上限还是惩罚权重，不能只比较数值大小。",en:"The original formulation minimizes residual sum of squares subject to an absolute-coefficient sum bounded by t. A smaller constraint bound means more shrinkage, unlike a penalty-weight formulation where a larger weight penalizes more. Software parameters must be identified by formulation before their numerical sizes are compared."},reference:{url:"https://sites.stat.washington.edu/courses/stat527/s13/readings/j_royal_stat_soc_b1996.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1996年期刊版，第268页",en:"Source: 1996 journal article, pp. 268"}}},{title:{zh:"变量尺度会改变惩罚含义",en:"Predictor scale changes the penalty's meaning"},body:{zh:"论文先将解释变量中心化并缩放到统一尺度。若一个字段以元计、另一个以百万元计，同样大小的系数惩罚并不代表同样的变量影响。用于新数据时应保留缩放规则，并在训练资料上确定变换，不能用后来观察到的信息改善历史预测。",en:"Predictors are centered and standardized before fitting. A coefficient penalty has a different meaning when one input is measured in units and another in millions. For new predictive applications, preserve scaling rules and estimate transformations from training data rather than using later observations to improve historical predictions."},reference:{url:"https://sites.stat.washington.edu/courses/stat527/s13/readings/j_royal_stat_soc_b1996.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1996年期刊版，第268页",en:"Source: 1996 journal article, pp. 268"}}},{title:{zh:"零系数来自收缩，不是显著性裁决",en:"A zero coefficient is not a significance verdict"},body:{zh:"在正交设计的说明中，Lasso表现为软阈值收缩：较小的系数被压至零，较大的也会缩小。这个例子帮助理解它与岭回归和子集选择的差异，但实际相关解释变量的情形更复杂。零系数不是证明某变量在经济上永远没有作用。",en:"In the orthonormal illustration, soft thresholding sets smaller coefficients to zero and shrinks larger ones. It clarifies differences from ridge regression and subset selection, but correlated predictors are more complicated. A zero fitted coefficient does not prove that a variable is economically irrelevant in every setting."},reference:{url:"https://sites.stat.washington.edu/courses/stat527/s13/readings/j_royal_stat_soc_b1996.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1996年期刊版，第269页",en:"Source: 1996 journal article, pp. 269"}}},{title:{zh:"调参目标是预测误差",en:"Tuning targets predictive error"},body:{zh:"论文讨论交叉验证、广义交叉验证等选择收缩程度的方法，并以非金融资料展示模型。验证方式决定参数选择回答什么问题。对有时间先后关系的金融数据，不能直接把独立观测示例中的分折程序当成已经处理了时间泄漏或市场制度变化。",en:"Cross-validation and generalized cross-validation help select shrinkage, illustrated with nonfinancial data. The validation design determines the question answered by tuning. For ordered financial observations, the independent-data example does not establish protection against temporal leakage or changing market regimes."},reference:{url:"https://sites.stat.washington.edu/courses/stat527/s13/readings/j_royal_stat_soc_b1996.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1996年期刊版，第273–275页",en:"Source: 1996 journal article, pp. 273–275"}}},{title:{zh:"固定参数与重新调参的不确定性不同",en:"Retuning introduces another source of uncertainty"},body:{zh:"论文比较自助样本中固定收缩参数与每次重新选择参数的标准误，后者加入额外的选择变化。报告一个固定模型的系数波动，不能自动概括完整建模流程的不确定性。解释结果时应说明是否重新调参，以及哪些步骤在重复样本中被固定。",en:"The example compares bootstrap standard errors with shrinkage held fixed and reselected in each sample; retuning adds selection variation. Variation around one fixed model does not automatically describe uncertainty in the full modeling procedure. State whether tuning is repeated and which steps remain fixed across samples."},reference:{url:"https://sites.stat.washington.edu/courses/stat527/s13/readings/j_royal_stat_soc_b1996.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1996年期刊版，第274–275页",en:"Source: 1996 journal article, pp. 274–275"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"Lasso的变量选择依赖缩放、样本和调参目标，不证明被选变量具有因果作用。原文的独立观测设定与示例不能直接替代金融时间序列的验证设计。",en:"Lasso selection depends on scaling, samples and tuning objectives; selected variables are not thereby causal. The paper's independent-observation setup and example do not replace validation designed for financial time series."}};export{e as default};
